  "ambiguities": [
    "The samples use customer names in paths, bill-to fields, contract parties, and email salutations that may be abbreviated or inconsistent; these should not be automatically merged.",
    "Technical document product codes and model values may appear crossed or inconsistent, such as GB-40 paired with model CS-110, VIS-200, or PS-4000. Preserve both values with their source context.",
    "The manual contains repeated instructions and apparent extraction artefacts such as question-mark bullets; repetition should not automatically be treated as separate instructions.",
    "Some emails say 'on the date above', but the supplied text does not contain an explicit date. Preserve the phrase and leave the scheduled date unresolved.",
    "Currency symbols differ across commercial documents, including pound and dollar symbols, and some symbols appear corrupted. Preserve the extracted symbol and avoid inferring currency solely from the supplier address.",
    "Delivery notes contain prices and totals, but the samples do not establish whether these are billing amounts or delivery valuation amounts.",
    "The term 'BILL TO' appears on delivery notes as well as invoices and quotations; it should not by itself determine the legal customer or contracting party.",
    "The quality report contains a title indicating non-conformance, but the listed findings do not clearly identify a specific non-conformance event or corrective action.",
    "File names may be truncated or contain inconsistent punctuation and should be retained separately from the document's internal identifiers.",
    "The samples include references to related drawings, schematics, schedules, and certificates that are not present in the supplied documents."
  ]
}